First, you need to be using some unix-like (or vax(?) or maybe other
things too, but -not- windows).  Then, it basically only knows how to check
the mail spool (no pop, imap, webmail, etc).  From there you just make sure
  #define MAIL
isn't commented out in unixconf.h and then recompile if needed.

>From there it'll periodically check to see if the file the enviro var MAIL
points to is changed or not and send a mail daemon after you if it has
been.  When you read a scroll of mail, it'll run the program referenced to
by MAILREADER.

